exports[`manifest template golden snapshots > renders each lazy add-on template with its stable anchor structure > lazy-before-after.md 1`] = `
"---
title: "Before/After Record: [NAME]"
description: "Level-agnostic record of what changed, why it changed and the resulting effect."
trigger_phrases:
  - "before after"
  - "change comparison"
  - "change record"
  - "migration comparison"
importance_tier: "normal"
contextType: "general"
---
# Before/After Record: [NAME]

<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: before-after | v2.2 -->
<!-- HVR_REFERENCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md -->

> [One line: what this record compares and why it matters.]

---

<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->
## 1. METADATA
<!-- FILL: Fill the document id, the date and the author. GOOD: BA-001, 2026-10-24, conductor. WEAK: TBD. -->

**Subject:** [SUBJECT]
**Status:** [Draft/Accepted/Archived]
**Date:** [YYYY-MM-DD]
**Owner:** [NAME OR ROLE]
**Related packet:** [PATH OR NONE]
<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->

---

<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->
## 2. SUMMARY
<!-- FILL: Write two sentences: what changed and the net effect. GOOD: The flag adds one line of output. The default path is unchanged. WEAK: A change was made. -->

**What changed:** [CONCISE DESCRIPTION OF THE CHANGE].

**Why it changed:** [THE DRIVER, PROBLEM OR DECISION THAT CAUSED IT].
<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->

---

<!-- ANCHOR:comparison -->
## 3. COMPARISON
<!-- FILL: Put the before and after side by side, one row per behavior. GOOD: Before: 17 lines. After with the flag: 1 line. WEAK: Before and after differ. -->

Write one block per aspect the change touched. Name the aspect, state how it was, then state how it is now. Keep it prose. Do not use a table.

**[ASPECT]**
Before: [PREVIOUS STATE].
After: [CURRENT STATE].

**[ASPECT]**
Before: [PREVIOUS STATE].
After: [CURRENT STATE].
<!-- /ANCHOR:comparison -->

---

<!-- ANCHOR:net-effect -->
## 4. NET EFFECT
<!-- FILL: State the one effect a reader should remember. GOOD: A caller can now read the level without parsing the report. WEAK: It is better. -->

**Behavior:** [WHAT A USER OR THE SYSTEM DOES DIFFERENTLY].
**Operational impact:** [RUNTIME, SUPPORT OR PROCESS EFFECT].
**Follow-up:** [REQUIRED FOLLOW-UP, OR NONE].
<!-- /ANCHOR:net-effect -->

---

<!-- ANCHOR:notes-caveats -->
## 5. NOTES & CAVEATS
<!-- FILL: Name one caveat and one thing not covered. GOOD: stderr is unchanged. No Windows test ran. WEAK: Some caveats apply. -->

[LIMIT, ASSUMPTION, EXCEPTION OR EVIDENCE NOTE. Write "None" if nothing applies.]
<!-- /ANCHOR:notes-caveats -->"
`;

